WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.709 --> 00:00:02.044
- This is it.
- Don't you die on me.

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.504
Don't count on it.

00:00:10.344 --> 00:00:11.553
If this whole thing ended,

00:00:11.637 --> 00:00:13.597
and there were only two pilots
left up in the air,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.724
it'd be me, and it'd be you, Buck.

00:00:16.266 --> 00:00:19.436
Today, the 8th will be sending up
three task forces.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:21.939
That's the largest air alma mater
ever assembled

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.191
- in the history of mankind.
- (men cheering)

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:27.653
Masters of the Air is about
a group of American airmen

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:29.404
who did what was asked of them.

00:00:29.488 --> 00:00:30.989
It's gonna to get bumpy.
Hang on, guys.

00:00:31.448 --> 00:00:32.449
Despite the chances,

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:35.410
they were either gonna get killed,
wounded or captured.

00:00:35.827 --> 00:00:37.621
I had thought it would be
easy to be in the sky

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:39.039
Rosenthal: Pilot to crew, flak ahead!

00:00:39.122 --> 00:00:41.458
There's dangers
that you don't really think about.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.671
There's more chance of you dying up there
than if you were down in the trenches.

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:47.798
These daylight missions are suicide.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:50.968
In the face of unimaginable mayhem…

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.219
Egan: Fighters, 12 o'clock!

00:00:52.302 --> 00:00:53.554
Nate Mann: …you have ten guys…

00:00:53.637 --> 00:00:55.305
Egan: Open fire!
Let 'em have it!

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:58.517
Nate Mann: …in a machine,
trying to keep it in the air.

00:00:59.476 --> 00:01:00.519
Any advice?

00:01:00.936 --> 00:01:02.104
Try to stay alive.

00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:03.605
Yes, sir.

00:01:03.689 --> 00:01:06.650
When you're in combat,
you know who you're fighting for?

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.694
The guy to your left
and the guy to your right.

00:01:09.444 --> 00:01:10.821
They have nothing but each other,

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:14.116
and they are able to conquer
anything when they stay together.

00:01:14.199 --> 00:01:15.242
(Men laughing and cheering)

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:16.159
Egan: Come on!

00:01:16.243 --> 00:01:18.370
I'm pretty sure that
this is the biggest production

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:19.454
any of us have ever done.

00:01:19.538 --> 00:01:20.873
Gary Goetzman: Definitely the hardest.

00:01:20.956 --> 00:01:22.666
Mission accomplished, boys.

00:01:22.749 --> 00:01:24.459
This has been my dream,
to do something like this.

00:01:24.543 --> 00:01:28.088
Let alone, with the team that made
Band of Brothers and The Pacific.

00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:29.715
Woohoo!

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.219
Austin Butler: And getting
to bring life to these heroic men,

00:01:34.303 --> 00:01:36.430
realizing how dangerous it was,

00:01:36.513 --> 00:01:38.974
and the bravery with which
they fought our freedom.

00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:41.226
That's the privilege for me,

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:43.812
and I hope that that's
what an audience receives.

00:01:43.896 --> 00:01:45.898
♪

00:01:45.981 --> 00:01:47.191
(mortar firing)

00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:48.567
(plane buzzing)

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:49.568
(explosions)

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:54.281
♪

